{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1070 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "011bb447e3453ddfc6b864032891a96eb61f136f80d4369b4a70f941ae1bbc58" :edb/db-before-t 1069 :edb/db-after-t 1070 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534382 50 #inst "2026-10-06T18:55:18.205Z" 13194139534382 true] [17592186171844 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285158 13194139534382 true] [17592186171845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285165 13194139534382 true] [17592186171845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285172 13194139534382 true] [17592186171846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285179 13194139534382 true] [17592186171846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186285186 13194139534382 true] [17592186285158 1017 #edb/ref 17592186285159 13194139534382 true] [17592186285158 1089 "q-107495" 13194139534382 true] [17592186285158 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534382 true] [17592186285158 1100 "Find the principal $20$th root of unity." 13194139534382 true] [17592186285158 1113 #uuid "78651eb4-8048-5b92-af07-f86f14c30c25" 13194139534382 true] [17592186285158 1145 "Let $z$ be a $20$th root of unity. This means that \n\n$$\n{z}^{20}=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the complex number $1$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta }.$ Notice that $|1|=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(1)=0.$ Hence, \n\n$$\n1={e}^{\\text{i}(0+2k\\pi )}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is an integer. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{20}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}}\\,⟹\\,z=({e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}})^{1/20}={e}^{k\\pi \\text{i}/10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe principal root corresponds to $k=1,$ and is therefore equal to ${e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/10}.$" 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285160 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285161 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285162 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285163 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1000 #edb/ref 17592186285164 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534382 true] [17592186285159 1041 "selection" 13194139534